---
source: tests/snapshots.rs
expression: help_for(&args)
---
Card or ACH credit payment (POST /v2/transactions/credit)

Usage: flute2 transactions credit [OPTIONS] --amount <AMOUNT> --payment-processor-id <PAYMENT_PROCESSOR_ID> --reference-id <REFERENCE_ID>

Options:
      --amount <AMOUNT>
          Transaction amount (required). Plain decimal, e.g. `500.00`
      --payment-processor-id <PAYMENT_PROCESSOR_ID>
          Payment processor UUID (required)
      --reference-id <REFERENCE_ID>
          Merchant-assigned reference ID for idempotency tracking (required)
      --currency-code <CURRENCY_CODE>
          Currency code, e.g. `USD`
      --customer-id <CUSTOMER_ID>
          Customer UUID for vault-linked credits
      --card <CARD>
          Card PAN (primary account number), e.g. `4111111111111111`
      --exp <EXP>
          Card expiry in MM/YY or MM/YYYY format, e.g. `12/26`
      --cvv <CVV>
          Card CVV/security code
      --payment-method-id <PAYMENT_METHOD_ID>
          Payment method UUID (stored card or bank account) to charge instead of raw details
      --instrument <INSTRUMENT>
          Which container `--payment-method-id` belongs in: `card` or `ach` [possible values: card, ach]
      --ach-account-number <ACH_ACCOUNT_NUMBER>
          Bank account number
      --ach-routing-number <ACH_ROUTING_NUMBER>
          Routing number (ABA)
      --ach-account-type <ACH_ACCOUNT_TYPE>
          Account type: `checking` or `savings` [possible values: checking, savings]
      --ach-account-holder-type <ACH_ACCOUNT_HOLDER_TYPE>
          Account holder type: `business` or `personal` [possible values: business, personal]
      --ach-tax-id <ACH_TAX_ID>
          Tax ID (optional)
      --sec-code <SEC_CODE>
          ACH SEC code: `web`, `ppd` or `ccd`. Required for ACH [possible values: web, ppd, ccd]
      --requester-ip <REQUESTER_IP>
          End-customer IP address. Default `127.0.0.1`. Required for ACH
      --same-day
          Request same-day settlement
      --contact-first-name <FIRST_NAME>
          Contact first name
      --contact-last-name <LAST_NAME>
          Contact last name
      --contact-company <COMPANY_NAME>
          Contact company name
      --contact-email <EMAIL>
          Contact email address
      --contact-phone <MOBILE_PHONE_NUMBER>
          Contact mobile/phone number in E.164 form. Required for new bank details
      --contact-sms-consent
          Record the contact's consent to receive SMS
      --billing-line1 <LINE1>
          AVS billing street line 1
      --billing-line2 <LINE2>
          AVS billing street line 2
      --billing-city <CITY>
          AVS billing city
      --billing-state <STATE>
          AVS billing state code (e.g. `CO`)
      --billing-postal-code <POSTAL_CODE>
          AVS billing postal / ZIP code
      --billing-country <COUNTRY>
          AVS billing country code (e.g. `US`)
      --shipping-line1 <LINE1>
          Shipping street line 1
      --shipping-line2 <LINE2>
          Shipping street line 2
      --shipping-city <CITY>
          Shipping city
      --shipping-state <STATE>
          Shipping state code (e.g. `CO`)
      --shipping-postal-code <POSTAL_CODE>
          Shipping postal / ZIP code
      --shipping-country <COUNTRY>
          Shipping country code (e.g. `US`)
  -h, --help
          Print help

Global options:
      --profile <PROFILE>  Active profile (environment). `sandbox` (default) or `production`/`prod` [env: FLUTE2_PROFILE=]
      --output <OUTPUT>    Output format: table (default), json, or quiet (id only). When omitted, falls back to the `FLUTE2_OUTPUT` env var, then to the `output` key in ~/.flute2/config.toml, then to `table` [env: FLUTE2_OUTPUT=] [possible values: table, json, quiet]
      --debug              Print HTTP request/response traces to stderr. Card and bank-account numbers are masked to the last 4 digits; CVV/security codes are removed
